UPDATE companies SET description='Louisiana Tech University was founded on July 6, 1894, in Ruston, Louisiana, as a public institution.

It operates on a quarter system, with a total enrollment of 12,039 students and a student-faculty ratio of 21:1. The campus centers on a pedestrian-friendly quad in Ruston, a town of approximately 22,000 residents.

Louisiana Tech serves students preparing for careers in engineering, business, health sciences, liberal arts, and applied sciences. The school partners with employers such as Big Four accounting firms and regional industry for internships, co-ops, and workforce development initiatives.

