UPDATE companies SET description='MADE Apparel Services was founded in 2020 by Heather Zager in Renton, Washington. Zager’s path to founding the company began with a patternmaking course in 2014, followed by an Associate of Applied Science in Apparel Design and Development from Seattle Central College. She spent two years at Meta integrating electronics and haptic components into wearable sewn products, and now teaches patternmaking and fit at her alma mater while also developing her own patent‑pending product, Zcissors.

The consultancy delivers end‑to‑end product development for sewn goods: pattern development using CLO3D and Alvanon digital forms, sewn prototyping with production‑intent construction, pattern grading via industry‑standard CAD tools, and comprehensive tech packs that organize bills of materials, construction sequences, and stitch specifications. A two‑person team — Zager and administrative support Nirosha Rodrigo — operates from a Seattle‑area base, guiding clients through each stage with a structured, transparent workflow.

Clients range from early‑stage startups to established brands and corporate teams. Projects have spanned equestrian apparel (Whinny Equestrian), postpartum recovery garments (Luna Azzurra Care), sustainable womenswear (Springtime & Harvest), supportive sports bras (Wrax), and functional accessories such as the Book Carrier Bookmark. The firm also draws on Zager’s wearable‑technology background to support soft‑goods concepts that incorporate sensors or electronics.

Zager started MADE to give creators a clear, organized path from concept to manufacture, emphasizing collaboration, respect, and inclusivity. The company’s differentiator is its focus on delivering production‑ready documentation alongside the practical knowledge clients need to make confident decisions as they scale.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pattern Development", "Sewn Prototyping", "Pattern Grading", "Tech Pack Creation", "Apparel Consulting", "Product Development Consulting", "3D Garment Simulation (CLO3D)", "Digital Pattern Making", "Fit Evaluation using Alvanon Forms"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Sewn Products", "Soft Goods", "Wearable Technology", "Equestrian Apparel", "Postpartum Recovery Garments", "Women''s Apparel", "Sports Bras", "Accessories"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CLO3D", "Alvanon Digital Forms", "Industry-Standard CAD Tools"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Structured, transparent development workflow from concept to production-ready deliverables", "Professional 3D simulation (CLO3D) and Alvanon digital forms for early fit evaluation", "Production-intent sewn prototypes with detailed review and pattern refinements", "Comprehensive tech packs organized to factory standards for fewer errors and faster turnaround", "Founder\u2019s firsthand experience launching a patent\u2011pending product and teaching at college level"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 -> /about", "Headquarters in Renton, Washington -> db", "Founder Heather Zager -> /about", "Services: pattern development, sewn prototyping, pattern grading, tech packs, apparel consulting -> /services", "Tools: CLO3D, Alvanon digital forms, industry-standard CAD -> /services, /", "Team includes Heather Zager and Nirosha Rodrigo -> /about", "Client examples: Whinny Equestrian, Luna Azzurra Care, Springtime & Harvest, Wrax, The Book Carrier Bookmark -> /", "Heather Zager background: 10+ years experience, Meta wearable tech, teaches at Seattle Central College, patent-pending Zcissors -> /about", "Company description: sewn product development consultancy -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "MADE Apparel Services is a sewn product development consultancy providing support to startups, established brands, and corporate teams developing apparel and sewn products.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='made-apparel-services' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MAGNA Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded on August 1, 1990, in Louisville, Kentucky, as a family-owned United States pharmaceutical company. Dr. Warren P. Lesser serves as president and chief executive officer, guiding the business with a stated commitment to accountability and community responsibility.

The company develops and manufactures pharmaceutical products and dietary supplements, with a focus on unique, non-substitutable formulations. Its flagship product, Stahist T, contains the antihistamine triprolidine and is formulated as scored tablets to allow half-tablet dosing for customized patient therapy.

The firm maintains memberships in the Wound, Ostomy, and Continence Nurses Society and the Specialty Pharma Association, indicating engagement with wound-care, ostomy, and continence nursing specialties as well as the broader specialty pharmaceutical market.

The company’s stated mission is to provide non-substitutable products and services at reasonable prices with genuine concern for stakeholders. Dr. Lesser has emphasized that the business exists to help people rather than solely to generate profit, a philosophy reflected in the “accountability” tagline incorporated into the corporate logo.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pharmaceutical manufacturing", "Supplement manufacturing"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Healthcare", "Wound care", "Ostomy care", "Continence care", "Specialty pharmaceuticals"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned structure with accountability as a core value", "Non-substitutable pharmaceutical formulations at reasonable prices", "Scored tablets enabling half-tablet, customized dosing", "Membership in Wound, Ostomy, and Continence Nurses Society and Specialty Pharma Association"], "facts_used": ["Founded August 1, 1990 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky -> /about-us", "Family-owned business -> /about-us", "Dr. Warren P. Lesser, President & CEO -> /about-us", "Specializes in pharmaceutical products and supplements -> /about-us", "Product Stahist T (Triprolidine) antihistamine -> db", "Tablets scored for half-tablet dosing -> db", "Member of Wound, Ostomy, and Continence Nurses Society -> /about-us", "Member of Specialty Pharma Association -> /about-us", "Mission: non-substitutable products at reasonable prices with genuine concern -> /about-us", "Tagline accountability -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in unique high-quality pharmaceutical products and supplements", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='magna-pharmaceuticals-inc' A