UPDATE companies SET description='MCT Industries Inc. was founded in 1974 in Albuquerque, New Mexico, as a family-owned and operated business. The company began with trailer sales and repairs and has since expanded into a full-service provider for truck bodies, trailers, and heavy equipment.

Today, MCT operates a custom fabrication facility equipped with a plasma cutter, laser cutter, 20-foot press brake, and shear. The company installs and customizes flatbeds, service bodies, dump bodies, and crane bodies, and provides hydraulic system service, refuse vehicle maintenance, DOT inspections, and snow-removal equipment installation such as salt spreaders and plows. It also supplies wetline kits, combo kits, walking-floor systems, end-dump trailers, and spray kits for herbicide and water trucks. A government manufacturing division handles design, prototype development, and full-rate production of items including nuclear and chemical munitions transporters, self-propelled ground support equipment, and large-scale plant fabrication. The parts department stocks more than 10,000 components for over 200 equipment types, and the company offers equipment rentals and roll-off waste services.

MCT serves state, city, and county agencies and municipalities, holding several State and CES contracts. Its government division works with military and federal customers, while its commercial division supports fleets, heavy-equipment operators, and construction contractors. The waste division provides roll-off service in the Albuquerque area and residential service in Santa Fe.

The company emphasizes its four-decade track record and a parts team experienced in locating hard-to-find components. Its government manufacturing plant highlights a capability to take projects from concept through full-rate production, a differentiator noted in its own materials.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication", "Installation and customization of flatbeds, service bodies, dump bodies, crane bodies", "Hydraulic system service and installation", "Refuse vehicle and equipment service", "Dump body installation", "DOT inspections", "Snow plow and salt spreader installation", "Wetline kit and combo kit installation for dump trucks, trailers, walking floors, end dumps", "Spray kit installation for herbicide and water trucks", "Trailer manufacturing (custom trailers)", "Equipment rentals (heavy duty trailers, equipment)", "Parts sales (over 10,000 parts)", "Trailer sales (light and heavy duty)", "Trailer repairs", "Roll-off waste service", "Residential waste service", "Government manufacturing: design, prototype development, full-rate production", "Nuclear and chemical munitions transporter fabrication", "Self-propelled ground support equipment fabrication", "Large-scale plant fabrication and construction", "Plasma cutting", "Laser cutting", "Press brake forming (20'')", "Shearing"], "industries": ["State, city, and county government entities", "Municipalities", "Military and federal government", "Waste management and refuse services", "Road construction", "Truck and trailer transportation", "Heavy equipment", "Nuclear and chemical munitions transport", "Ground support equipment", "Large-scale plant fabrication"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Plasma cutter", "Laser cutter", "20'' press brake", "Shear"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 10,000 parts stocked for 200+ equipment and trailer types", "Family-owned and operated since 1974", "Holder of multiple State and CES contracts for government entities", "Government manufacturing plant offering design-to-production services for defense and industrial projects", "Custom fabrication shop with plasma cutter, laser cutter, 20'' press brake, and shear"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 in Albuquerque, NM -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "Custom fabrication with plasma cutter, laser cutter, 20'' press brake, shear -> /", "Stocks over 10,000 parts for 200+ equipment types -> /", "Installs flatbeds, service bodies, dump bodies, crane bodies -> /", "Provides hydraulic systems, refuse vehicle service, DOT inspections -> /", "Snow plow and salt spreader installation -> /", "Wetline kits, combo kits, walking floors, end dumps, spray kits -> /", "Government manufacturing plant for design to full-rate production -> /about", "Nuclear/chemical munitions transporters, ground support equipment, plant fabrication -> /about", "State and CES contracts holder -> /", "Services state, city, county entities and municipalities -> /", "Waste division: roll-off service Albuquerque, residential Santa Fe -> /about", "Equipment rentals -> /", "Trailer sales and repairs -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MCT''s Government manufacturing plant works with our customers from design and prototype development to full rate production", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mct-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MEI Electrical Contractors & Systems Integrators is based in Westfield, Vermont. The company traces its roots to 1991 when it was founded as Mike’s Electric, Inc. in Jay, Vermont. A branch office opened in Williston in 2013 to serve Chittenden County and western Vermont. The fire alarm and security divisions were spun off as MEI Systems Integrators in 2014. In 2017, then‑President Adam Fortier acquired the business and relocated it to a larger facility in Westfield.

Today MEI provides full‑service electrical contracting along with fire alarm and security system design, installation, maintenance, testing, inspection, repair, and monitoring. The firm employs over 65 people, including master and journeyman electricians, certified fire alarm and security technicians, project managers, designers, and estimators. Its capabilities span design/build projects, lighting design and conservation, electrical service upgrades, 24‑hour emergency response, network infrastructure, access control, video surveillance, and fiber optics. Project experience ranges from residential generator installations to multi‑million‑dollar commercial and industrial new construction, including solar and renewable energy work.

MEI serves commercial, industrial, health care, educational, agricultural, governmental (federal, state, and local), and residential customers throughout Vermont and New Hampshire, with government contracts extending into New York, Maine, and Massachusetts. Long‑standing general‑contractor partners include DEW Construction Corp., PeakCM LLC, Bread Loaf Corporation, ReArch Company, Wright & Morrissey Inc., and Kingsbury Companies.

The company emphasizes a “Site Management Strategy” to coordinate schedules, priorities, and participants for turn‑key delivery, and it operates a Customer Alarm Portal for system monitoring. MEI participates in the Vermont Registered Apprenticeship program to train new electricians and highlights its safety record and continuous training. Its stated mission is to provide efficient, quality work on time and on budget while fostering a family‑focused workplace with advancement opportunities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical system design, installation, maintenance, testing, inspection, repair", "Fire alarm system design, installation, maintenance, testing, inspection, repair, monitoring", "Security system design, installation, maintenance, testing, inspection, repair, monitoring", "Design/build project delivery", "Lighting design and energy conservation", "Electrical service upgrades", "24\u2011hour emergency response", "Network infrastructure installation", "Access control systems", "Video surveillance systems", "Fiber optic cabling", "Solar and renewable energy system installation"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Health Care", "Educational", "Agricultural", "Governmental (Federal, State, Local)", "Residential"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24\u2011hour emergency service", "Vermont Registered Apprenticeship program for electrician training", "Multi\u2011year state and federal government contracts", "Site Management Strategy for project coordination", "Customer Alarm Portal for remote monitoring"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1991 as Mike''s Electric, Inc. in Jay, VT -> /about", "Branch office opened in Williston, VT in 2013 -> /about", "Fire alarm and security divisions spun off as MEI Systems Integrators in 2014 -> /about", "Adam Fortier purchased business in 2017 and moved headquarters to Westfield, VT -> /about", "Employs over 65 employees, many 