UPDATE companies SET description='MEI Industrial Solutions operates from Southbridge, Massachusetts, where it runs a fabrication facility and retail metal shop. The business was formerly known as Accurate Metal Sales & Fabrication before adopting its current name.

The company provides custom metal fabrication, including sub-assemblies, weldments, structural repairs, and complex weldments, alongside retail sales of structural steel shapes. Its in-house design team uses SolidWorks and AutoCAD to produce 3D engineered drawings and conceptual blueprints. Fabrication processes cover MIG, TIG, and stick welding, CNC plasma cutting, oxyacetylene and plasma torch cutting, drilling, grinding, beveling, jigging, fit-up, and assembly. Equipment includes a high-definition plasma table cutting up to 1.5-inch mild steel, a hydraulic shear for 3/4-inch plate, a press brake bending 1/2-inch by 10-foot lengths, roll forms, an ironworker, and various welding machines. Services are offered both in-house and on-site, with rigging and installation of finished products.

MEI serves the commercial construction industry, municipal governments, residential general contractors, and the general public. Its welders hold AWS D1.1 structural certification and MIL certification for military and defense contracts, allowing the shop to take on defense-related work.

The company emphasizes its certified welding staff and advanced CNC plasma cutting as key differentiators, aiming to meet exact client requirements and delivery deadlines. Its retail operation sells metal with no minimum quantity, accommodating orders from a single piece to full truckloads.', certifications=ARRAY['AWS D1.1','MIL certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail metal sales", "Custom metal fabrication", "In-house design (SolidWorks, AutoCAD)", "3D engineered drawings", "Structural repairs", "Complex weldments", "Rigging and installation", "CNC plasma cutting", "MIG/TIG/Stick welding", "AWS D1.1 certified welding", "MIL certified welding", "Weld inspection and quality control", "Cutting, drilling, grinding, beveling", "Oxyacetylene cutting", "Plasma torch cutting", "Jigging, fit-up and assembly", "On-site fabrication services"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Municipal government", "Residential construction", "Military and defense", "General public"], "materials": ["Mild steel", "Hot rolled steel", "Structural steel"], "equipment": ["Hi Def Plasma Table (cuts up to 1.5 inch mild steel)", "Hydraulic Shear (shear up to 3/4\" mild steel)", "Vertical Band Saw (cut 18\" x 18\")", "Radial Arm Drill (drill bits up to 3\")", "Press Brake (bend up to 1/2\" mild steel by 10'' long)", "Small Roll Form (roll 1/4\" x 4ft wide)", "Large Roll Form (roll 3/8\" x 8ft wide)", "Iron Worker (punch up to 1.25\" dia thru 3/4\" mild steel)", "MIG, TIG, and Stick welding machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All welders certified to AWS D1.1 and MIL standards", "In-house design with SolidWorks and AutoCAD", "CNC plasma cutting up to 1.5-inch mild steel", "On-site and in-house fabrication services", "Retail metal sales with no minimum order (one piece to truckload)"], "facts_used": ["Company name, location, former name, description -> db", "Capabilities list -> db", "Products list -> db", "Address, contact, hours, detailed capabilities, equipment, inventory, retail info -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "MEI provides retail metal sales and custom metal fabrication, sub-assemblies and weldments to the general public as well as the commercial construction industry, municipalities and residential general contractors.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mei-industrial-solutions-providence' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MGM Transformers, based in Vernon, California, has been designing and building transformers since 1974. The company operates as a subsidiary of Forgent, a platform that brings together over 100 years of experience in power infrastructure.

The company manufactures dry-type transformers using vacuum pressure impregnation (VPI) and cast coil epoxy resin processes, as well as liquid-filled padmount and substation transformers. It also produces power distribution unit (PDU) transformers for data centers and general-purpose low-voltage transformers. Operations span five advanced production facilities totaling 1.5 million square feet across California, Texas, and Tijuana, Mexico, with a vertically integrated manufacturing model and approximately 1,500 employees.

MGM Transformers serves data centers from hyperscale to edge deployments, grid modernization projects including solar, storage, and utility-scale infrastructure, and industrial manufacturing facilities requiring process loads, electrification, and plant resilience. Its transformers are also used in commercial, industrial, and utility applications; a noted customer is Standard Solar, which received a grounding transformer in four weeks.

