UPDATE companies SET description='MRL Equipment Company operates from Billings, Montana, where it has manufactured pavement marking, removal, grooving, and pavement maintenance equipment for over 36 years. The business was founded by road stripers who brought first-hand knowledge of striping and removal operations to the design of their machines. No explicit founding year or ownership structure beyond the founders'' background is disclosed.

The company produces a range of specialized trucks and systems for road marking and surface preparation. Its product line includes thermoplastic trucks with 12,000 lb and 16,000 lb capacity, the EpoxyPro™ plural component impingement material mixing system, multiple-head progressive removal and grooving trucks, and road marking and raised pavement marker (RPM) application equipment. The firm also offers parts, support, and retrofit services for existing fleets. Facility size, headcount, and annual production volumes are not publicly stated.

The equipment is built for high-volume output, serviceability, and ease of operation in striping, removal, grooving, and raised marker applications across highway and roadway projects.

