UPDATE companies SET description='Machined In Wood operates from Bellingham, Massachusetts. The shop began as a small, home-based business and has since expanded to serve both individual clients and commercial manufacturers. No founding year or founder names are disclosed in public sources.

The company provides custom CNC woodworking, laser engraving, and finishing services. Its equipment includes two 48" x 48" CNC routers (one with pass-through capability), a horizontal boring machine, CO2 and diode laser engravers, and a 3D printer. Traditional woodworking tools such as a table saw, band saw, jointer, planer, drum sander, and router complement the digital fabrication. They handle production runs from dozens to hundreds of parts and maintain a 1% tolerance level with rigorous quality inspections.

Customers range from hobbyists and local wood shops to engineers and commercial firms requiring prototyping or small-to-medium scale manufacturing. The shop works with wood, plastic, acrylic, and aluminum, and offers painting and finishing including hand painting, airbrushing, HVLP, spar urethane, polyurethane, and nitrocellulose lacquer for musical instruments. They do not produce epoxy river tables or large-scale cabinetry.

Machined In Wood differentiates itself by investing in specialized equipment like the horizontal boring machine and large-format flattening capacity, allowing it to take on smaller, complex jobs that larger shops decline. The team emphasizes nearly two decades of experience collaborating with engineers, proficiency in GD&T, and a policy of not marking up customer-supplied material.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining (V carving, 3D carving, precision parts, profile cuts)", "Laser cutting", "Laser engraving", "3D printing", "Traditional woodworking (table saw, band saw, jointer, planer, drum sander, router, sanding)", "Painting and finishing (hand painting, airbrushing, HVLP, stain, clear coat, food-grade finishes)", "Design and consultation", "CAD/CAM", "Photogrammetry", "3D modeling", "Small to medium run production manufacturing", "Photo carving"], "industries": ["Custom woodworking", "Prototyping", "Small-to-medium manufacturing", "Musical instrument finishing", "Hobbyist and maker support", "Engineering and design collaboration", "Commercial manufacturing"], "materials": ["Wood", "Plastic", "Acrylic", "Aluminum", "Plywood", "Pine", "Oak"], "equipment": ["48\" x 48\" CNC router (2 units, one pass-through)", "Horizontal boring machine", "CO2 laser engraver", "Diode laser engraver", "3D printer", "Table saw", "Band saw", "Jointer", "Planer", "Drum sander", "Router", "HVLP paint system"], "volume": "Dozens to hundreds of parts per run; small to medium scale manufacturing", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "1% tolerance level", "built_on": ["Horizontal boring machine for precise horizontal holes", "CNC flattening capacity up to 48\" x 48\"", "Focus on smaller, complex jobs larger shops decline", "1% tolerance with rigorous QA inspections", "Nearly 20 years experience with engineers and GD&T"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bellingham, MA -> db", "Home-based business origin -> homepage", "Two 48\"x48\" CNC machines (one pass-through) -> homepage", "Horizontal boring machine -> homepage", "CO2 and Diode laser engravers -> homepage", "3D printing capability -> homepage", "Production runs dozens to hundreds -> homepage", "1% tolerance level with QA -> homepage", "Nearly two decades experience with engineers -> homepage", "Accept customer-supplied material, no markup -> homepage", "Finishing services: hand painting, airbrushing, HVLP, Spar Urethane, polyurethane, nitrocellulose lacquer -> homepage", "Industries: individuals, wood shops, makers, commercial, engineers -> homepage", "Instagram @machined_in_wood -> homepage", "Website machinedinwood.com -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Machined In Wood is a custom CNC woodworking shop that specializes in CNC machined wood projects, laser engraving, and finishing of custom one of a kind pieces, prototypes, and small to medium scale manufacturing.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://instagram.com/machined_in_wood"], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='machined-in-wood' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mack Molding was founded in 1920 and is headquartered in Arlington, Vermont, with additional facilities in East Arlington and Cavendish, Vermont, as well as Inman, South Carolina, and Statesville, North Carolina. The company operates as a vertically integrated contract manufacturer across ten locations totaling more than 1.5 million square feet of manufacturing space.

The company provides custom plastic injection molding from 28- to 4,000-ton presses with shot sizes up to 769 ounces, supporting volumes from five pieces to five million annually. Capabilities include large-part molding, structural foam, gas-assist, and two-shot molding, complemented by in-house tooling, CNC machining, sheet metal fabrication (laser cutting, bending, welding), Class A painting, pad printing, ultrasonic welding, and turnkey electromechanical assembly up to Class III medical devices.

Mack serves customers in the medical, industrial, transportation, robotics, energy and utilities, and defense sectors, ranging from Fortune 500 corporations to private enterprises. Its vertically integrated model allows coordination of plastic and metal components from a single location, reducing lead times and ensuring quality across complex programs.

The company emphasizes financial stability — debt-free with a 5A1 Dun & Bradstreet rating — and positions itself as a single partner with total responsibility, leveraging over a century of experience, ITAR and FDA registrations, and certifications including ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, ISO 14001:2015, and IATF 16949:2016.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','ISO 14001:2015','IATF 16949:2016','FDA registered','ITAR registered','NIST SP 800-171 (CMMC Level 2 Self-Assessed)','JCP Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic Injection Molding", "Large Part Molding", "Structural Foam Molding", "Gas-Assist Molding", "Two-Shot Molding", "Class A Painting", "Pad Printing", "Ultrasonic Welding", "Heat Staking", "CNC Milling", "CNC Turning", "Laser Cutting", "CNC Forming / Press Brakes", "Welding", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Design for Assembly (DFA)", "Design for Testing (DFT)", "Rapid Prototyping", "Soft Tooling", "3D Printing", "Mechanical Assembly", "Electronic Assembly", "Electromechanical Assembly", "Clean Room Molding", "Automated Assembly", "Supply Chain Management", "Fulfillment & Logistics", "Program Launch Management", "In-House Tooling"], "industries": ["Medical", "Industrial", "Transportation", "Robotics", "Energy & Utilities", "Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["120+ injection molding presses (28\u20134,000 ton)"], "volume": "5 to 5 million units annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Debt-free with 5A1 D&B rating", "10 facilities, 1.5M+ sq ft manufacturing space", "120+ injection molding presses (28\u20134,000 ton)", "Vertically integrated design-to-fulfillment under one roof", "ITAR registered and FDA registered for defense and medical work"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1920 -> db", "Headquarters Arlington, VT -> /", "Facilities: 10 locations, 1.5M+ sq ft -> /", "120+ injection molding presses 28-4,000 ton -> /", "Shot sizes 0.6-769 oz -> /", "Volumes 5 to 5 million -> /", "Capabilitie