UPDATE companies SET description='Majestic Metals was founded in 1979 in Denver, Colorado. For more than 45 years the shop has built a reputation for service, quality, and speed in sheet metal fabrication. Now operating as Majestic Metals by Fathom, the facility continues to serve customers across the Denver region and nationwide from its original location.

The Denver facility provides end-to-end sheet metal fabrication, taking parts from laser cutting and CNC punching through forming, welding, captive hardware installation, finishing, graphics, and final assembly. Equipment includes three fiber and solid-state lasers, two CO2 lasers, five punch presses, thirteen press brakes up to 12 feet and 220 tons, twelve TIG welders, seven MIG welders, and a laser welder. The shop runs lights-out production for quantities of 100 to 10,000 parts and supports projects from prototype through full production.

Core industries include data centers and IT infrastructure, EV charging equipment, medical device housings, self-service kiosks and retail technology, industrial equipment enclosures, military and defense, automotive, energy, agriculture, semiconductor, and consumer electronics and lighting. Customers receive complete fabricated products such as server cabinets, equipment enclosures, control panels, EV charging stations, and analytical equipment.

The company differentiates itself with a single-source model that eliminates multi-vendor friction, a value-engineering approach on every project, design-for-manufacturability support, and a 98% on-time delivery rate. The facility is ISO 9001 certified and ITAR registered, allowing it to handle government and defense work.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision laser cutting", "CNC punching", "Forming and bending (press brake)", "Welding (arc, MIG, TIG, spot, laser)", "Captive hardware installation", "Painting", "Powder coating", "Screen printing", "Mechanical assembly", "Kitting", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "CNC machining", "Laser inspection", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Value engineering", "Lights-out production"], "industries": ["Data centers and IT infrastructure", "EV charging equipment", "Medical device housings", "Self-service kiosks and retail technology", "Industrial equipment enclosures", "Military and defense", "Automotive", "Energy", "Agriculture", "Semiconductor", "Consumer electronics and lighting"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["Fiber lasers", "Solid-state lasers", "CO2 lasers", "Punch presses", "Press brakes (13 machines, up to 12 ft, 220 tons)", "TIG welders (12)", "MIG welders (7)", "Laser welder", "Automated loading and unloading equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.005 in", "built_on": ["Single-source fabrication, finishing, graphics, and assembly under one roof", "Lights-out production for 100\u201310,000 parts", "Design-for-manufacturability support on every project", "98% on-time delivery", "ISO 9001 certified and ITAR registered"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 -> /", "Headquarters Denver, Colorado -> /", "ISO 9001 certified -> /", "ITAR registered -> /", "Single-source model: fabrication, finishing, graphics, assembly under one roof -> /", "Laser cutting tolerance \u00b10.005 in -> /", "