UPDATE companies SET description='Maple Lane Farms operates from Charleston, Maine, on a property first purchased by Stanley Higgins in 1935. The farm passed to Charles “Shine” and Margaret Higgins in 1941, became Charles C Higgins & Son in the 1960s, and was renamed Maple Lane Farms in 1999 when Barry and Mary Higgins bought the operation. It remains a fifth‑generation family‑owned business run by the Higgins family.

A state‑inspected processing facility, expanded in 2005 and again in 2011 to add refrigeration and an automated smoke house, handles custom slaughter and cutting for customers’ own animals as well as the farm’s own stock. Products are hand‑cut, sealed, and flash‑frozen with no aged inventory. The farm also produces and sells horse‑quality round and square hay bales (stored indoors and net‑wrapped), silage by the ton, and screened compost made from processing, cow, and horse waste.

Customers include local households purchasing retail cuts through the on‑farm store (open Monday–Friday with call‑in ordering), farmers needing custom processing for their livestock, horse owners seeking hay, and gardeners using the compost. The business historically served wholesale channels but now focuses on direct‑to‑consumer and custom‑processing sales.

The Higgins family diversified into meat processing, hay, and compost to keep the farm viable amid changing regulations and market pressures. They emphasize that every step — from cutting to labeling — is done by hand, not by high‑speed automation, and that products go straight from the cutting room to the freezer to ensure freshness.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom meat processing (beef, pork, lamb, chicken)", "State\u2011inspected slaughter and cutting", "Flash freezing", "Automated smoke house operation", "Hay production and sales (round and square bales)", "Silage production and sales", "Screened compost production", "Retail meat sales (sides, quarters, whole, individual cuts)", "Call\u2011in order fulfillment with callback notification", "Curbside pickup and in\u2011store shopping"], "industries": ["Livestock farming", "Meat processing", "Hay and forage", "Compost and soil amendments", "Retail food sales"], "materials": ["Beef cattle", "Pork", "Chicken", "Lamb", "Hay", "Silage", "Compost (processing waste, cow waste, horse barn waste)"], "equipment": ["Automated smoke house"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand\u2011crafted processing: every cut, seal, and label done by hand", "Flash\u2011frozen immediately after cutting \u2014 no old stock", "State\u2011inspected facility with automated smoke house", "One of the largest hay dealers in the Northeastern U.S.", "Accepts EBT, cash, check, credit, and debit"], "facts_used": ["Location: Charleston, ME -> /", "Founding: Stanley Higgins bought farm in 1935 -> /about", "Ownership: Family-owned, Higgins family -> /about", "Renamed Maple Lane Farms in 1999 -> /about", "700 cows typically -> /about", "State-inspected processing facility -> /about, /", "Facility expansions 2005 and 2011 (refrigeration, automated smoke house) -> /about", "Hand-cut, sealed, flash-frozen -> /", "Hay: round/square bales, horse quality, stored indoors -> /, /about", "Silage s