UPDATE companies SET description='Mar-Med was founded in 1989 in Grand Rapids, Michigan, by Dr. Joseph Marogil, a general surgeon who invented the Tourni-Cot digital tourniquet to address a need he encountered in hand surgery cases. The company remains physician-founded and family-owned.

Today Mar-Med operates as an FDA-registered medical device manufacturing site certified to ISO 13485:2016. It designs and distributes a line of disposable devices including the Tourni-Cot and Uni-Cot digit tourniquets, the Rhino-Pak epistaxis balloon, the Balloon Extractor for nasal foreign-body removal, the Derma-Stent abscess and cyst drain, and the ZEROWET wound irrigation system. The company serves emergency medicine, podiatry, pediatrics, orthopedic surgery, and other specialties, shipping to healthcare facilities worldwide.

Mar-Med''s customer base spans hospital emergency departments, surgical centers, and clinics across the U.S. and internationally. Its products are used in procedures ranging from digit laceration repair to epistaxis control and nasal foreign-body extraction.

The company states its mission is to create growth and opportunity in its community through the manufacture and distribution of effective medical devices that support efficient procedures, positive patient outcomes, and a healthy bottom line. Mar-Med also emphasizes sustainability, composting label backing paper, recycling eligible waste, and reusing cardboard and scrap paper.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA QSR (21 CFR Part 820)','CE Mark (MDD 93/42/EEC)','CE Mark (MDR EU 2017/745)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device manufacturing", "Product design and development", "Global distribution", "Quality management system (ISO 13485:2016)", "FDA QSR compliance (21 CFR Part 820)", "CE marking (EU MDR)", "Sustainable manufacturing practices (composting, recycling, reuse)"], "industries": ["Emergency medicine", "Podiatry", "Pediatrics", "Orthopedic surgery", "Healthcare facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Physician-founded, family-owned since 1989", "FDA-registered manufacturing site with ISO 13485:2016 certification", "Designs and distributes novel disposable medical devices for multiple specialties", "Sustainability program including composting, recycling, and reuse of manufacturing byproducts", "Recent acquisition of ZEROWET wound irrigation line"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 in Grand Rapids, Michigan by Dr. Joseph Marogil -> /about-us", "Physician founded, family owned -> /about-us, /", "FDA registered manufacturing site certified to ISO 13485:2016 -> /about-us, /quality", "Products: Tourni-Cot, Uni-Cot, Rhino-Pak, Balloon Extractor, Derma-Stent, ZEROWET -> /", "Serves emergency medicine, podiatry, pediatrics, orthopedic surgery -> /about-us", "Global distributor to healthcare facilities worldwide -> /about-us", "Mission: create growth and opportunity through effective medical devices -> /about-us", "Sustainability: composting, recycling, reuse -> /about-us", "Acqu