UPDATE companies SET description='Md Plastics Inc. was founded in 1999 by Mike Durina in Columbiana, Ohio, drawing on his decades of experience in plasticating technology. The company began as a specialist in designing and manufacturing high-performance plasticating components for injection molding and extrusion processes.

Today the firm produces a full range of precision plasticating components—injection molding screws, extrusion feed screws, non-return valves, plasticating barrels, and nozzle tips—along with patented systems such as the INJECT-EX™ plasticating and injection units, the Melt-IQ™ and Melt-Profiler™ II real-time melt monitoring systems, and large-scale pellet-fed 3D printers. All components are engineered using proprietary design software that calculates heat transfer, shear rates, and pressure profiles for each application. The company also offers vented barrel conversions, injection unit upsizing and downsizing, and purging compounds.

Md Plastics serves automotive, medical device, consumer electronics, additive manufacturing, and general plastic processing sectors. Its customer base includes major equipment builders such as Absolute Haitian, Engel, Milacron, and Windsor, who integrate the company’s components and monitoring systems into their machines.

The company was established to help injection, extrusion, blow molding, and 3D printing operations become more profitable through better plasticating components and entirely new technologies. Its differentiation rests on nine granted patents, proprietary analytical software, and closed-loop melt monitoring that converts real-time temperature data into thermodynamic work analysis for unprecedented part consistency.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding screw design and manufacturing", "Extrusion feed screw design and manufacturing", "Non-return valve manufacturing", "Plasticating barrel manufacturing", "Nozzle tip manufacturing", "Plasticating system design (INJECT-EX)", "Melt monitoring systems (Melt-IQ, Melt-Profiler II)", "Vented barrel design", "Injection unit upsizing and downsizing", "Large scale pellet-fed 3D printer manufacturing", "Purging compound formulation", "Process control and predictive analytics", "Custom plasticating component engineering", "Retrofit integration with existing equipment", "Installation support and operator training"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical Devices", "Consumer Electronics", "Additive Manufacturing", "Plastic Processing", "OEM"], "materials": ["PE", "PP", "PVC", "ABS", "PC", "PET", "Engineering plastics", "Hygroscopic ionomers"], "equipment": ["INJECT-EX\u2122 Machine", "INJECT-EX\u2122 for 3D Printing", "INJECT-EX\u2122 for LSR", "INJECT-EX\u2122 for Thermoplastics", "Melt-IQ\u2122 System", "Melt-Profiler\u2122 II System", "Mini-Shut\u2122 Automatic Shut-Off Nozzle", "Posi-Melt\u2122 3D Printing Screws", "Posi-Melt\u2122 Extrusion Screws", "Posi-Melt\u2122 MB Barrier Screws", "Posi-Melt\u2122 Multipurpose Screws", "Posi-Melt\u2122 XLA Mixing Screws", "Posi-Shut\u2122 Automatic Shut-Off Valve", "MDP\u2122 Performance Non-Return Valve", "Temp-Sense\u2122 Melt Sensor"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nine granted patents covering plasticat