UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1994 in Leadville, Colorado, Melanzana Outdoor Clothing began as a local apparel manufacturer committed to domestic production. The founders chose Leadville for its affordable cost of living and outdoor lifestyle, building a workforce from the small mountain community.

The company designs, cuts, and sews its own line of outdoor apparel—including hoodies, base layers, and accessories—from factories in Leadville and Alamosa.

Melanzana sells directly to consumers through its Leadville store and online shop, serving outdoor enthusiasts, hikers, and mountain-town residents. The brand has become a staple in the Colorado outdoor community, with products used by local nonprofits and trail organizations that the company supports through giving programs.

The company distinguishes itself by keeping production in Colorado, using predominantly U.S.-made fabrics, and operating as an employee-owned business. Its founding principle was to avoid outsourcing and provide good local jobs, a mission that continues to drive its expansion to Alamosa and its community giving programs such as PB & Melly and 1% For The Outdoors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cut and sew apparel manufacturing", "Apparel design and development", "Fabric sourcing and testing (primarily U.S.-made)", "Direct-to-consumer retail and e-commerce", "Factory tours"], "industries": ["Outdoor recreation", "Apparel manufacturing"], "materials": ["Merino wool", "U.S.-made fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1994 in Leadville, Colorado -> /about", "Dedicated to local manufacturing, not outsourcing -> /about", "Over 80 employees in Leadville, 40 in Alamosa -> /about", "Employee-owned with over 20 employees holding stock -> /about", "Designed and sold over 50 original products -> /about", "Uses primarily U.S.-made fabrics, with Merino wool from Thailand -> /about", "Community programs: PB & Melly, 1% For The Outdoors, annual donations over $60,000 -> /about", "Operates retail store in Leadville and online store -> /", "Factory tours available -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a LOCAL manufacturer.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "120+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='melanzana-outdoor-clothing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mercer Spring & Wire Co operates from Townville, Pennsylvania, where it has been producing springs for over 70 years. The company does not disclose its exact founding year or ownership structure, but its longevity reflects deep experience in cold-formed spring manufacturing.

The shop specializes in cold-wound compression, torsion, and extension springs, as well as wire forms, working with wire diameters from 0.008 to 0.500 inches. Materials include music wire, hard-drawn and oil-tempered spring wire, 302 and 316 stainless steel, beryllium copper, and various round and rectangular profiles. The facility is ISO 9001:2015 certified, and all products are made in the United States.

Mercer Spring serves the automotive, electrical switchgear, safety equipment, air/gas/refrigeration, and medical equipment sectors, along with a miscellaneous industrial customer base. The company emphasizes custom spring orders and works closely with clients on design and quality.

