UPDATE companies SET description='Mercury Plastics MD operates from Baltimore, Maryland, as the East Coast division of Mercury Plastics Inc., a Midwest-based custom thermoformer with 65 years of history. The Maryland division traces its roots to 1984 and was formerly known as Maryland Thermoform Corporation (MTC) before joining the Mercury family in February 2018 under General Manager Carl Livesay.

The facility provides vertically integrated thermoforming, plastic fabrication, printing, overmolding, and in-house extrusion services. It handles projects from custom prototypes to high-volume packaging runs, supported by CNC machining, tool-and-die capabilities, and a 5S lean manufacturing program. The plant uses MX4 maintenance software and recycles all plastic scrap, metals, and corrugated waste.

Customers span candle packaging — notably Candle Packaging USA, one of the nation’s largest producers — and medical/first-responder sectors, for which the company produced 30,000 face shields during the COVID-19 pandemic. The firm also serves general industrial and packaging markets with heavy-gauge thermoformed parts.

Mercury Plastics MD differentiates itself through vertical integration that keeps projects in-house, lead times claimed to be up to five times faster than competitors, and a sustainability focus that includes recycled and biodegradable materials plus proprietary extrusion development. A culture of collaboration and thought partnership is cited as key to solving complex challenges.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Vacuum thermoforming", "Heavy-gauge thermoforming", "Plastic fabrication", "Printing services", "Overmolding", "In-house extrusion", "CNC machining", "Tool and die making", "Prototyping", "High-volume packaging", "5S lean manufacturing", "MX4 preventive maintenance", "Scrap recycling (plastics, metals, corrugated)", "Material sourcing and inventory management", "Design for manufacturability assistance", "Quality inspection and testing"], "industries": ["Candle packaging", "Medical/first responder", "Industrial packaging", "General industrial"], "materials": ["Recycled plastics", "Reprocessed plastics", "Blended plastics", "Biodegradable plastics", "Proprietary extruded materials"], "equipment": ["MX4 maintenance software", "CNC machining equipment", "Tool and die equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated, wholly American-made production", "Lead times up to 5x faster than competitors", "In-house extrusion and proprietary material development", "5S lean manufacturing with MX4 maintenance software", "Full recycling of plastic scrap, metals, and corrugated materials"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 -> db", "Headquarters Baltimore, Maryland -> db", "ISO 9001 certified -> db", "Division of Mercury Plastics Inc. -> /about", "Formerly Maryland Thermoform Corporation (MTC) since February 2018 -> /about", "Vertical integration and wholly American-made -> /about", "Capabilities: thermoforming, fabrication, printing, overmolding, extrusion -> /about", "Lead times up to 5x faster -> /about", "5S lean manufacturing program -> /about", "MX4 maintenance software -> /about", "Recycling all plastic scrap, metals, corrugated -> /about", "In-house extrusion of proprietary materials -> /about", "Candle Packaging USA client -> /about", "30,000 face shields for first responders -> /about", "Team members: Carl Livesay, James Hall, Scott Kneebone, Lakyn Pieper, Matthew Livesay, Dan Scroggins -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a manufacturer, Mercury Plastics, Inc. offers unparalleled expertise in Thermoforming, Plastic Fabrication, and Printing Services", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mercury-plastics-md' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1967 in Spencer, Massachusetts, Mercury Wire Products Inc has operated as a custom wire and cable manufacturer for over five decades. The company serves customers nationwide and globally from its Massachusetts base.

Mercury Wire designs and manufactures engineered wire, cable, and assembly solutions tailored to specific applications. Its services span custom cable manufacturing, full cable assembly, custom engineering, and rapid in-house prototyping. Production follows lean principles with dedicated value stream teams that own projects from design through delivery, supported by Kanban inventory management and pull-based systems. The company scales from prototype runs to full production programs without stating facility size or headcount.

The company serves medical, aerospace, industrial, and specialty markets. Concrete examples include a global inspection company using waterproof push-rod cables for sewer and pipeline environments, a leader in plasma cutting technology improving plasma cutter leads, and a manufacturer of analytical instrumentation reducing field failures. Customers also include OEMs in power, signal, and specialty applications.

Mercury Wire differentiates itself through a people-first, continuous-improvement culture. Its DIVE process (Design optimization, Inventory management, Value stream integration, Execution excellence) aims to accelerate value velocity. The company emphasizes direct customer access to the build team, rapid prototyping with agile decisions, and a partnership model described as ''large enough to meet demand and small enough to stay personal.''', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR','REACH/RoHS','UL (Application-Specific)','CSA (Application-Specific)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable design and manufacturing", "Cable assembly and integration", "Custom engineering and prototyping", "Design optimization for manufacturability", "Rapid in-house prototyping", "Lean manufacturing and value stream management", "Kanban inventory management", "Rigorous testing and quality assurance", "Scalable production from prototype to full volume", "Material selection, shielding, and jacketing", "Turnkey assembly solutions", "Precision crimping and termination", "DIVE process (Design, Inventory, Value stream, Execution)"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Industrial", "Sewer and pipeline inspection", "Analytical instrumentation", "Power and signal applications", "Specialty applications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to full production", "lead_time": "Rapid prototyping and flexible production; lead times shortened via lean processes", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dedicated value stream teams own projects end-to-end, eliminating handoffs", "Lean manufacturing and continuous-improvement culture prioritizing value velocity", "Rapid in-house prototyping with agile decisions by the build team", "Kanban and pull-based inventory management for steady supply chain", "Direct access to the team that built the product for ongoing support"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1967, Spencer, MA -> db, /", "Custom cable manufacturer since 1967 -> /", "Certifications: ITAR, ROHS -> db; REACH/RoHS, UL, CSA, ITAR Registered -> /", "Capabilities: custom cable manufacturing, assembly, engineering, prototyping -> /, /services", "Industries: medical, aerospace, plasma cutting, sewer/pipeline inspection, analytical instrumentation -> /", "Value stream teams, lean, Kanban, DIVE process -> /, /about-us", "Scalable production prototype to production -> /, /about-us", "Personalized service, direct access to build team -> /", "No founders, ownership, employee count, facility size, equipment, tolerances, min order, languages, social links stated -> /, /about-us, /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mercury Wire is a custom cable manufacturer specializing in engineered wire, cable, and assembly solutions built for your specific application and environment.", "founded_year": "1967", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mercury-wire-products-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Meridian Cable, LLC, headquartered in St. Augustine, Florida, opened its first facility in 1994. The company operates two production sites: a 7,000-square-foot plant in St. Augustine and a 30,000-square-foot facility in Tanggu, China, which it owns outright. President Bud Kinzalow leads the organization.

The company designs and manufactures custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, coil cords, overmolded assemblies, RF cable assemblies, and shielded cable assemblies. Its capabilities span custom cable design and engineering, custom extrusion (from 34 AWG to 12 AWG), overmolding and insert molding using low-pressure molding machines such as the LPMS Beta 300, prototyping, pre-production testing, qualification sampling, and volume manufacturing. Meridian designs more than 70 percent of the products it builds and maintains a tooling inventory of over 5,000 molds for connectors, junctions, overmolds, and housings.

Its customers require custom solutions that cannot be sourced off the shelf, and the company supports them from concept through production with services that include KanBan and stocking programs.

